# Copy to backend/.env (or a repo-root .env) and fill in.
# Never commit the filled-in file.

# ── Required ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Model provider key. Read by the Pydantic AI process only — it never reaches
# the browser, because the browser never talks to the agent server directly.
OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-...


# ── Backend, optional ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Model id for every agent, in Pydantic AI's "provider:model" form.
# Defaults to `openai:gpt-4.1-mini`, the id the Quickstart prints. The Tool
# Rendering and Shared State pages print `openai:gpt-5.4-mini`, which OpenAI
# does not serve — set this if you want to test whatever the docs currently show.
# OPENAI_MODEL=openai:gpt-4.1-mini

# Port for the agent server. Change this and PYDANTIC_AI_AGENT_URL together.
# AGENT_PORT=8000

# Origins allowed to call the agent server directly. Only matters if you bypass
# the runtime; the normal path is server-to-server and needs no CORS.
# AGENT_CORS_ORIGINS=http://localhost:3000,http://127.0.0.1:3000


# ── Frontend, optional ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# These belong in frontend/.env.local (Next.js does not read this file).

# Base URL the runtime uses to reach the agent server. Each agent is mounted at
# <base>/<agent_id>/. Use 127.0.0.1 if localhost resolves to IPv6 while the
# agent binds IPv4.
# PYDANTIC_AI_AGENT_URL=http://localhost:8000

# ── CopilotKit Intelligence ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Both are read SERVER-SIDE by the runtime route
# (frontend/src/app/api/copilotkit/[[...slug]]/route.ts) and belong in
# frontend/.env.local. Neither is NEXT_PUBLIC_ — a browser-prefixed key would
# ship in the JS bundle.
#
# They are two independent axes, and the connection panel on `/` reports them on
# separate rows because a runtime can have one without the other:

# 1. The project key. Turns the runtime from SSE mode into Intelligence mode:
#    /info reports mode "intelligence", threads persist, and rename/archive/
#    delete get a real endpoint. Without it an in-memory runner backs the
#    threads, chat still works everywhere, and nothing survives a restart.
# INTELLIGENCE_API_KEY=cpk-...

# 2. The license token. Independent of the key above. /info derives
#    `licenseStatus` from it, and client-side feature UIs gate on THAT field —
#    <CopilotThreadsDrawer> shows its locked Upgrade view unless the status is
#    valid or expiring, even when threads are working perfectly.
# COPILOTKIT_LICENSE_TOKEN=...

# Identity for `identifyUser` on the runtime, sent as headers by Providers.
# Threads are per-user; without a stable identity every visitor shares one
# history. Change the id to watch two thread lists diverge.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_DEMO_USER_ID=harness-local
# NEXT_PUBLIC_DEMO_USER_NAME=Harness User

# Origin the server-side /info probe calls itself on. Only needed if the app is
# not on http://127.0.0.1:$PORT.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_ORIGIN=http://localhost:3000

# Opt out of CopilotKit's anonymous runtime telemetry.
# COPILOTKIT_TELEMETRY_DISABLED=true
